A||||2||WisconsinGT||Cam removal question||||1||
Z||000000||WisconsinGT||08-05-2000||11:21 PM||||I was wondering if it would be possible to remove the camshaft on our 2.8's through the rear wheelwell. I am sure it is not possible but I thought I would bring it up, to see what y'all thought. Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||08-06-2000||10:44 AM||||I would think that you could do that procedure if you loosened the front 'K' member bolts and removed the ones in back and jack the rear of the car up. It seems possible but I have never tried it. If you do let me know if it works! Like I said, seems like it should!<BR>You may have to remove the nuts from the upper strut mounts also in order to get enough 'swing' for clearance.<BR>Be sure to use jack stands and something to support the "K" member on the passenger side.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Taijiguy||08-06-2000||12:18 PM||||Obviously, the first best choice would be to pull the motor, but the second best may be to try and tilt the motor upwards in front. I wonder if there's enough room for that? You'd have to disconnect the manifolds from the exhaust pipes, and disconnect the front engine mount as well as the side torque strut, hmmmm...guess you'd have to also loosen or remove the coolant cross pipe.....hmmmm, OK, may it's not such a great idea after all. Just pull the sucker, and yank the motor so you can replace the cam bearings while you're in there....<BR>Or, just do whatever you want. I have to go now.....<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>-Taiji||||reg||3
